// A for-in over a value that is not a List, String, Map, or Coroutine is a
// fatal fault. A try does not catch it, so the catch block and the code after
// the try never run (spec/04-semantics.md, Fatal Runtime Errors). The program
// prints nothing and exits with status 70.
try {
    for (var x in 5) { print x; }
} catch (e) {
    print e.kind;
}
print "after";

// STATUS: error
// EXIT: 70
